MANIFOLD afternoon VERSION 1
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AFTERNOON fixture — a faithful minimal world for *The Theory of Data in One Afternoon*.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. `specs/doctrine_gaps.md` DG-2 forward invariant 5 requires that the system EXPRESS
# the Afternoon case: attempt a temporal SUM of a base stock; find no lawful temporal-sum reading;
# REFUSE, naming the reason and the lawful neighbours. Until 2026-08-20 there was no fixture in this
# repository to run that against — the Afternoon existed only as prose in the ledger — so the
# invariant could not be certified, only asserted. This is that fixture.
#
# WHAT IT IS. The smallest world that carries the Afternoon's shape: a stock measured as a daily
# snapshot per store, a flow measured per order, two lineages (one temporal, one geographic) so the
# law can be shown to be PER LINEAGE rather than per measure, and a derived family so the laundering
# class can be exercised through a carrier. Deliberately tiny and hand-checkable: every number a test
# asserts can be recomputed by eye from `afternoon_world.py`.
#
# THE DECLARED LAW. `on_hand` bars temporal `sum` and nothing else (ruling 2026-08-20 §6: do not
# infer a global stock personality; applicability stays per operator × lineage). So:
#   · summing `on_hand` across CALENDAR is structurally prohibited — in every spelling;
#   · summing `on_hand` across STORES is lawful, because the bar names `calendar`, not the measure;
#   · averaging, min-ing, max-ing and counting `on_hand` over time remain lawful, because the author
#     barred `sum` and did not bar those. That is a DECLARATION, not an oversight the engine repairs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

UNIVERSE sales = store * day * order   BASIS events
    -- "an order line: one store, one day, one order"
UNIVERSE stock_snapshot = store * day   BASIS spine
    -- "the daily on-hand snapshot, one row per store per day"

LEVEL store = store_id BASE   -- "a shop"
LEVEL day = day BASE          -- "a calendar day: the finest grain anyone can ask at"
LEVEL order = order_id BASE   -- "one order"
LEVEL region = region         -- "a group of shops"
LEVEL month = month           -- "a reporting month"

HIERARCHY geography { store -> region VIA stores(store_id, region) }   -- "shop geography"
HIERARCHY calendar  { day -> month VIA calendar(day, month) }          -- "the reporting calendar"

MEASURE revenue ON sales FROM sales_lines AS sum(amount)
    -- "money taken; a FLOW — it adds along every axis, which is exactly why it is the control"

MEASURE on_hand ON stock_snapshot FROM inventory VALUE level
    -- "units on the shelf at the close of each day; a POSITION, not a flow"
    FAMILY {
        sum  BLOCKED { calendar }   -- "adding snapshots across days counts the same unit once per day"
        last ORDER day              -- "position = the latest snapshot in the period"
    }

DERIVED stock_pair = on_hand.last + on_hand.last
    -- "a binary MAP over a stock: a CARRIER for the laundering class, not a meaningful quantity"
